macOS: complete notifying commits through the existing outside-owner helper.

Cider-Topic: sync/msync
Cider-Requires: 0104-msync-thread-local-fork-admission.patch
Cider-Status: nondefault alternative branch, excluding0105-0107
Cider-Review-By: independent scoped journal/death/cancellation/fork review and parent
Cider-Test: production-header death/stale-helper/concurrency and notification scope;
 original under-owner path and omitted recovered-wake/sequence-guard negatives rejected

Preserve COMMITTED as the state decision and APPLIED until wake obligations are
actually delivered. All ten production commit callers synchronously finish.
Notifications use the existing helper after dropping this executor's owner;
other executors may hold it concurrently. Keep native frames, shared references,
leases, epoch validation, cancellation, registration and compare-before-park.
Return a matched completed helper with its refreshed CLEAN guard still held,
just as normal entry; newer journals retain leave/retry. No CLEAN-before-notify.
This adds common-path gate round trips and may duplicate advisory wakes. Three
uncontended acquisitions replace one, so a shorter hold is not proof of speed.
Paired native builds and new runtime/performance/hour results are required.

--- a/include/wine/msync_coord.h
+++ b/include/wine/msync_coord.h
@@ -352,7 +352,12 @@
             guard->token = coord->get_token ? coord->get_token() : token;
             msync_coord_take( guard );
             if (header->sequence == sequence && header->state == MSYNC_COORD_APPLIED)
+            {
                 __atomic_store_n( &header->state, MSYNC_COORD_CLEAN, __ATOMIC_RELEASE );
+                /* Already own a clean gate with refreshed admission/lease.
+                 * Return under that guard, just like the normal CLEAN entry. */
+                return;
+            }
             msync_coord_leave( guard );
             continue;
         }
@@ -394,10 +399,11 @@
         __atomic_store_n( (uint64_t *)slot, entries[i].value, __ATOMIC_RELEASE );
     }
     __atomic_store_n( &header->state, MSYNC_COORD_APPLIED, __ATOMIC_RELEASE );
-    /* Usual path: no extra lock round trips. The pump never takes this gate,
-     * and a zero-timeout send cannot wait for its queue to drain. */
+    /* Preserve APPLIED until the existing helper path delivers every wake
+     * outside this gate. Callers synchronously finish before returning; a dead
+     * helper leaves the journal recoverable, never CLEAN-before-notify. */
     for (i = 0; i < count; ++i)
-        if (entries[i].notify && !coord->notify( entries[i].idx, coord->slot( entries[i].idx, 0 ), 0 )) return;
+        if (entries[i].notify) return;
     __atomic_store_n( &header->state, MSYNC_COORD_CLEAN, __ATOMIC_RELEASE );
 }
 
